---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { contact } from '../content/site';

/**
 * Terms for a marketing site: no accounts, no payments, no downloads, nothing
 * to log into. Kept to what's actually true of this site rather than padded
 * out with clauses about services it doesn't offer.
 *
 * Two things here are the owner's call and were flagged at the time of
 * writing: the governing-law line, and whether a registered legal entity name
 * should appear instead of "Thread".
 */
const updated = '13 August 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms · Thread"
  description="The terms that apply to using threadhawaii.com: what's on it, what it is and isn't, and where the actual agreement for a project lives."
>
  <Header />

  <section class="legal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Terms of use.</h1>
      <div class="eyebrow">Terms</div>
      <p class="lead" style="max-width:56ch">
        These cover this website. They are not the terms of a project. Those live in a
        written proposal, signed before any work starts.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site is</h2>
      <p>
        threadhawaii.com describes Thread, a custom software practice based in Honolulu.
        Everything on it is descriptive. Nothing on it is an offer, a quote, or a promise
        of a particular result.
      </p>

      <h2>The drawings are drawings</h2>
      <p>
        The plates on this site are marked as concept drawings and specimens. They
        illustrate the kind of thing Thread builds and the shape of what a systems map
        contains. They are not screenshots of any client's software, and the businesses,
        figures and workflows in them are illustrative.
      </p>

      <h2>The systems map</h2>
      <p>
        The map is offered free, limited to two a month and one workflow each. Requesting
        one does not commit you to anything, and it does not commit Thread to taking the
        work on. If more requests arrive than can be honoured, they are taken in order and
        you will be told where you stand rather than left waiting.
      </p>

      <h2>Work Thread takes on</h2>
      <p>
        Any actual engagement is governed by a written proposal covering scope, price,
        timing and ownership. Where that proposal and this website disagree, the proposal
        wins.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy</h2>
      <p>
        This site is kept accurate and current as far as is reasonable, but it is provided
        as it is, without warranty. Thread is not liable for loss arising from relying on
        the general information here rather than on advice given about your specific
        situation.
      </p>

      <h2>Content</h2>
      <p>
        The text, drawings and design on this site belong to Thread. You are welcome to
        quote or link to any of it with attribution. Please don't republish the plates or
        the page design wholesale as your own.
      </p>

      <h2>Links elsewhere</h2>
      <p>
        Where this site names other companies' products, it does so descriptively. Those
        names belong to their owners, and naming them implies no partnership, endorsement
        or certification in either direction.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Hawaiʻi.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Base>
